The Rive runtimes are consumed unmodified as dependencies — RiveRuntime
through the plugin's podspec, app.rive:rive-android through Gradle — so no
line of their source is copied or changed here. From rive-flutter and
rive_native the plugin mirrors Dart API names only (the fit, alignment and
hit-test enums, the input and event names), so that code written against them
moves across with the import swap.

The example app contains code adapted from rive-flutter. It rebuilds
rive-flutter's example app screen for screen (example/lib/rive_examples/):
the menu, section and screen names, descriptions and .riv files are theirs,
and each ported screen — example/lib/rive_examples/screens/*.dart and
example/lib/rive_official/*.dart — is adapted from the matching file under
rive-flutter/example/lib/examples/ (0.15.0-dev.3), re-expressed against this
plugin's API, with a header naming its source and what changed. That code is
covered by rive-flutter's MIT licence, reproduced below, and ships with the
example only, never with the plugin package.

The example also bundles sample .riv files from Rive's own example apps, so
its screens can be compared against theirs. Every file is byte-identical to
its upstream copy. From rive-ios's Example-iOS/Assets: Bear.riv,
artboard_animations.riv, leg_day_events_example.riv, light_switch.riv,
rating_animation.riv, testtext.riv, truck.riv. From rive-flutter's
example/assets: ball_elements.riv, button.riv, coyote.riv,
data_binding_lists.riv, electrified_button_nested_text.riv, focus.riv,
hit_test_consume.riv, layout_test.riv, lip-sync.riv, lists_demo.riv,
little_machine.riv, multitouch.riv, off_road_car.riv, rating.riv, rewards.riv,
rive_rendering_test.riv, semantic_list_scroll_focus_fixed.riv, semantics.riv,
skills.riv, tabtest.riv, travel_icons_pack.riv, url_event_button.riv,
vehicles.riv, web_icons_pack.riv, zero_area_semantics.riv, and the three
out-of-band files acqua_text_out_of_band.riv, image_out_of_band.riv and
ping_pong_audio_demo.riv (lip-sync.riv and off_road_car.riv also ship in
rive-ios's assets, unchanged). They carry no separate asset licence and are
covered by the MIT licences of those repositories, reproduced below. They
ship with the example only, never with the plugin package.

The example also bundles the three audio clips ping_pong_audio_demo.riv
references out of band — racket1-59343.wav, racket2-59344.wav and
table-59328.wav — taken unchanged from rive-flutter's example/assets/audio
and covered by the same MIT licence. The out-of-band screens fetch their
fonts and images at runtime, as upstream's do (fonts from cdn.rive.app,
images from picsum.photos); none of those are bundled.

The example also bundles one font, Inter-Regular.ttf (version 3.019), which
acqua_text_out_of_band.riv references out of band, taken from rive-flutter's
example/assets/fonts. Inter is by The Inter Project Authors under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1, reproduced below; the font's own name table carries
the same notice. The images and sounds upstream's out-of-band screens use
are not bundled: the ports fetch them by URL at run time.

The example also bundles four files from the Rive Marketplace, all under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence and unmodified (see their entries
below, and NOTICE.md beside them): example/assets/rive/marketplace/
audio_player.riv, "Audio Player" by RiottersDesign, which embeds the font
Inter Tight (SIL Open Font License 1.1, reproduced below) and three music
tracks credited in its entry; example/assets/rive/marketplace/
studiorun.riv, "StudioRun - A Cosmic Game by TheLittleLabs" by thelittlelabs,
which embeds the font Inter (same licence), six images and 40 sounds;
example/assets/rive/marketplace/big_wheel.riv, "Big Wheel Demo" by JcToon,
which embeds the font Londrina Solid (same licence) and one sound; and
example/assets/rive/marketplace/sleep_onboarding.riv, "Sleep onboarding
screen" by marciofpantoja, UI design and illustration by Afsar Hossen, which
embeds the font Inter (same licence). The licence's full text is in
example/assets/rive/marketplace/LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt, and the font
licence's in OFL-1.1.txt beside it. They ship with the example only, never
with the plugin package.

The example's example/assets/rive/marketplace/dragon_ball.riv is
DartNative's own, written by example/tool/dragon_ball/build.sh from a trace
of an image generated with Craiyon
(https://www.craiyon.com/fr/image/ngkUyMYoSyKO_gBOI_zQ6Q). It leaves out
Craiyon's logo; as Craiyon's terms accept, its screen credits Craiyon in text
instead. It embeds example/assets/rive/marketplace/dragonball_sound_4s.mp3,
the sound dragonball_sound.mp3 beside it from its fourth second on: "Anime
Powerup (Dragonball becoming Super Saiyan) - Sound Effect for editing" by
Sound Library (2023), credited on the screen.

